    {
      "id": "ann_fr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 3010,
      "width": 1065.626953125,
      "height": 55.199999999999996,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2Y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 415924773,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1867106213,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784359811608,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "FR: (1) Low-code bot authoring with visual topic editor (2) Generative AI answers grounded in enterprise KB (3) 1400+ connectors via Power Automate (4) Multi-channel: Teams/Web/Slack/IVR\n     (5) Live agent handoff with full transcript (6) Adaptive Card responses (7) Custom entity extraction (8) Plugin/action execution (9) ALM: Dev→Test→Prod promotion\nNFR: (1) 99.9% SLA (bot runtime) (2) P50 < 1.5s, P95 < 4s (generative), P50 < 500ms (topic match) (3) 600 msg/min/bot rate limit (4) Tenant isolation per Dataverse environment\n     (5) Data residency: geo-bound to Power Platform region (6) Compliance: SOC2, ISO27001, HIPAA eligible (7) DLP policy enforcement per connector (8) Auto-scale: 0→N based on message volume",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "FR: (1) Low-code bot authoring with visual topic editor (2) Generative AI answers grounded in enterprise KB (3) 1400+ connectors via Power Automate (4) Multi-channel: Teams/Web/Slack/IVR\n     (5) Live agent handoff with full transcript (6) Adaptive Card responses (7) Custom entity extraction (8) Plugin/action execution (9) ALM: Dev→Test→Prod promotion\nNFR: (1) 99.9% SLA (bot runtime) (2) P50 < 1.5s, P95 < 4s (generative), P50 < 500ms (topic match) (3) 600 msg/min/bot rate limit (4) Tenant isolation per Dataverse environment\n     (5) Data residency: geo-bound to Power Platform region (6) Compliance: SOC2, ISO27001, HIPAA eligible (7) DLP policy enforcement per connector (8) Auto-scale: 0→N based on message volume",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "syncedAt": "2026-07-18T12:43:10.902Z",
      "source": "frontend_sync",
      "syncTimestamp": "2026-07-18T12:43:10.887Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "ann_math",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 3100,
      "width": 849.123046875,
      "height": 55.199999999999996,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2Z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 280092331,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1490268459,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784359811608,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "SCALE MATH: Avg enterprise: 50 bots, 10K conversations/day/bot | Platform: ~500K active bots globally | Peak: ~50M conversations/day\nTokens: 8K avg/conv × 50M = 400B tokens/day | Cost/conv: $0.03 (KB hit) to $0.08 (gen answer) | Revenue: $200/bot/mo × 500K = $100M/mo\nKB indexing: 500 sources/bot × avg 50 pages × 512 tok chunks = ~50K chunks/bot | Index size: 50K × 6KB = 300MB/bot | Total: 500K × 300MB = ~150TB index\nRedis session: 50M conv/day × 2KB state × 30min TTL = ~700K concurrent entries × 2KB = ~1.4GB (fits in Premium P2 13GB shard)",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "SCALE MATH: Avg enterprise: 50 bots, 10K conversations/day/bot | Platform: ~500K active bots globally | Peak: ~50M conversations/day\nTokens: 8K avg/conv × 50M = 400B tokens/day | Cost/conv: $0.03 (KB hit) to $0.08 (gen answer) | Revenue: $200/bot/mo × 500K = $100M/mo\nKB indexing: 500 sources/bot × avg 50 pages × 512 tok chunks = ~50K chunks/bot | Index size: 50K × 6KB = 300MB/bot | Total: 500K × 300MB = ~150TB index\nRedis session: 50M conv/day × 2KB state × 30min TTL = ~700K concurrent entries × 2KB = ~1.4GB (fits in Premium P2 13GB shard)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "syncedAt": "2026-07-18T12:43:10.902Z",
      "source": "frontend_sync",
      "syncTimestamp": "2026-07-18T12:43:10.887Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "ann_trade",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 3200,
      "width": 897.1123046875,
      "height": 227.7,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2a",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1927345541,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 341543685,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784359811609,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "TRADE-OFFS:\n1. Dataverse vs custom DB for bot config: ✓ Dataverse: native Power Platform ALM, security roles, solution packaging | ✗ Custom SQL: cheaper/RU but no ALM, no DLP, custom RBAC\n   Math: Dataverse included in license vs $500/mo custom DB + 1 FTE ($200K/yr) for ALM tooling. Decision: Dataverse wins on operational cost\n\n2. CLU vs GPT-only intent routing: ✓ Hybrid: CLU for trained intents (< 30ms) + GPT fallback (< 1.5s) | ✗ GPT-only: simpler but 5x slower, $0.005/classify\n   Math: 80% of queries match trained topics via CLU (30ms, $0) vs GPT ($0.005). At 50M conv/day: saves $200K/day by using CLU first\n\n3. Azure AI Search vs Cosmos DB vector: ✓ AI Search: native hybrid BM25+HNSW, semantic ranker, zero-ops | ✗ Cosmos: vector search newer, less mature ranker\n   Math: AI Search S2 = $700/mo/index vs Cosmos vector = $500/mo but no semantic ranker. 15% better NDCG justifies $200/mo premium\n\n4. Power Automate vs direct HTTP for actions: ✓ PA: 1400 pre-built connectors, visual flow editor, DLP | ✗ Direct HTTP: faster (no orchestration overhead), custom only\n   Math: PA adds ~300ms overhead but saves 10x dev time. 90% of enterprise actions use existing connectors (no code needed)\n\n5. Generative answers on/off toggle: ✓ Admin control per topic | ✗ Always-on: better coverage but hallucination risk\n   Math: Toggle-off for regulated topics (finance, legal) prevents 100% of gen hallucination in those areas. Acceptable 15% coverage gap\n\n6. Per-bot AI Search index vs shared index: ✓ Per-bot: tenant isolation, no cross-bot data leak | ✗ Shared: cheaper, easier to manage\n   Math: Per-bot S2 shard = $700/mo vs shared $70/mo amortized. Security justifies 10x cost for enterprise. Cross-bot leak = P0 incident",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "TRADE-OFFS:\n1. Dataverse vs custom DB for bot config: ✓ Dataverse: native Power Platform ALM, security roles, solution packaging | ✗ Custom SQL: cheaper/RU but no ALM, no DLP, custom RBAC\n   Math: Dataverse included in license vs $500/mo custom DB + 1 FTE ($200K/yr) for ALM tooling. Decision: Dataverse wins on operational cost\n\n2. CLU vs GPT-only intent routing: ✓ Hybrid: CLU for trained intents (< 30ms) + GPT fallback (< 1.5s) | ✗ GPT-only: simpler but 5x slower, $0.005/classify\n   Math: 80% of queries match trained topics via CLU (30ms, $0) vs GPT ($0.005). At 50M conv/day: saves $200K/day by using CLU first\n\n3. Azure AI Search vs Cosmos DB vector: ✓ AI Search: native hybrid BM25+HNSW, semantic ranker, zero-ops | ✗ Cosmos: vector search newer, less mature ranker\n   Math: AI Search S2 = $700/mo/index vs Cosmos vector = $500/mo but no semantic ranker. 15% better NDCG justifies $200/mo premium\n\n4. Power Automate vs direct HTTP for actions: ✓ PA: 1400 pre-built connectors, visual flow editor, DLP | ✗ Direct HTTP: faster (no orchestration overhead), custom only\n   Math: PA adds ~300ms overhead but saves 10x dev time. 90% of enterprise actions use existing connectors (no code needed)\n\n5. Generative answers on/off toggle: ✓ Admin control per topic | ✗ Always-on: better coverage but hallucination risk\n   Math: Toggle-off for regulated topics (finance, legal) prevents 100% of gen hallucination in those areas. Acceptable 15% coverage gap\n\n6. Per-bot AI Search index vs shared index: ✓ Per-bot: tenant isolation, no cross-bot data leak | ✗ Shared: cheaper, easier to manage\n   Math: Per-bot S2 shard = $700/mo vs shared $70/mo amortized. Security justifies 10x cost for enterprise. Cross-bot leak = P0 incident",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "syncedAt": "2026-07-18T12:43:10.902Z",
      "source": "frontend_sync",
      "syncTimestamp": "2026-07-18T12:43:10.887Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "ann_corner",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 3600,
      "width": 842.21435546875,
      "height": 101.19999999999999,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2b",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1610010955,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 423252939,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784359811609,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CORNER CASES:\nCC-1: Stale KB source (PDF updated but not re-indexed) → Webhook on SharePoint change triggers re-ingest pipeline. Fallback: show \"answer may be outdated\" disclaimer\nCC-2: Circular topic redirect (Topic A → B → C → A) → Max redirect depth = 10, engine breaks loop and returns fallback message\nCC-3: PII in generative answer (user’s SSN in HR bot) → Presidio PII detection in post-filter, redact before display, log for audit\nCC-4: Power Automate flow timeout (120s) → Return \"still processing\" card with refresh button, async callback writes result to Dataverse\nCC-5: Channel-specific card incompatibility (Slack doesn’t support Adaptive Cards v1.5) → Graceful fallback to plain text + buttons\nCC-6: Bot publish during active conversations → Blue-green deployment: new config loads on next conversation, active sessions use old config\nCC-7: DLP violation (bot tries to call blocked connector) → Runtime DLP check before connector invoke, return admin-configured error message",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CORNER CASES:\nCC-1: Stale KB source (PDF updated but not re-indexed) → Webhook on SharePoint change triggers re-ingest pipeline. Fallback: show \"answer may be outdated\" disclaimer\nCC-2: Circular topic redirect (Topic A → B → C → A) → Max redirect depth = 10, engine breaks loop and returns fallback message\nCC-3: PII in generative answer (user’s SSN in HR bot) → Presidio PII detection in post-filter, redact before display, log for audit\nCC-4: Power Automate flow timeout (120s) → Return \"still processing\" card with refresh button, async callback writes result to Dataverse\nCC-5: Channel-specific card incompatibility (Slack doesn’t support Adaptive Cards v1.5) → Graceful fallback to plain text + buttons\nCC-6: Bot publish during active conversations → Blue-green deployment: new config loads on next conversation, active sessions use old config\nCC-7: DLP violation (bot tries to call blocked connector) → Runtime DLP check before connector invoke, return admin-configured error message",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "syncedAt": "2026-07-18T12:43:10.902Z",
      "source": "frontend_sync",
      "syncTimestamp": "2026-07-18T12:43:10.887Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "ann_innov",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 3840,
      "width": 841.822265625,
      "height": 75.89999999999999,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2c",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1553071333,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1830675045,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784359811609,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "INNOVATIONS:\n1. Generative Actions: LLM auto-selects which Power Automate flow to call based on user intent (no manual topic→flow mapping). Reduces authoring time 80%\n2. Copilot Studio + M365 Copilot bridge: Custom plugins authored in Studio can extend M365 Copilot (single authoring surface, dual runtime)\n3. Autonomous Agent mode: Long-running agents that execute multi-step workflows without user prompts (event-triggered, e.g., \"when new hire onboards, run 5-step setup\")\n4. Multi-source grounding: Single generative answer can cite chunks from SharePoint + uploaded PDFs + Dataverse rows + website URLs simultaneously\n5. Conversation booster: Zero-config generative fallback — just add KB sources, no topic authoring needed. Reduces time-to-first-bot from weeks to minutes",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "INNOVATIONS:\n1. Generative Actions: LLM auto-selects which Power Automate flow to call based on user intent (no manual topic→flow mapping). Reduces authoring time 80%\n2. Copilot Studio + M365 Copilot bridge: Custom plugins authored in Studio can extend M365 Copilot (single authoring surface, dual runtime)\n3. Autonomous Agent mode: Long-running agents that execute multi-step workflows without user prompts (event-triggered, e.g., \"when new hire onboards, run 5-step setup\")\n4. Multi-source grounding: Single generative answer can cite chunks from SharePoint + uploaded PDFs + Dataverse rows + website URLs simultaneously\n5. Conversation booster: Zero-config generative fallback — just add KB sources, no topic authoring needed. Reduces time-to-first-bot from weeks to minutes",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "syncedAt": "2026-07-18T12:43:10.902Z",
      "source": "frontend_sync",
      "syncTimestamp": "2026-07-18T12:43:10.887Z"
    },
