    {
      "id": "07IzGAjalN5xxpQaf1GSR",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1862.7850826023946,
      "y": 484.0063055965136,
      "width": 548.0195922851562,
      "height": 975,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2i",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1937222155,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1503463563,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784374936915,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "OMNICHANNEL FLOW (Slack / Facebook / IVR)\nStep-by-Step:\n\n1. User sends message on Slack/FB/phone\n2. Channel adapter receives via per-channel webhook\n   • Slack: Events API POST (JSON payload)\n   • Facebook: Messenger webhook (PAGE_TOKEN)\n   • IVR: Azure Communication Services (SIP trunk)\n3. Adapter normalizes to Bot Framework Activity\nschema\n   • Activity.type = \"message\"\n   • Activity.channelId = \"slack\" | \"facebook\" |\n\"telephony\"\n   • Attachments mapped to BF Attachment schema\n4. Normalized Activity → Azure Bot Service\n(HTTPS/443)\n5. Bot Service routes to Bot Runtime Gateway (by bot\nregistration ID)\n6. Gateway loads session from Redis (key: session:\n{botId}:{convId})\n   • If new conversation: create session, load bot\nconfig from Dataverse\n   • If existing: resume dialog state from Redis\n7. Dialog Engine executes (same pipeline as Teams)\n8. Response Activity generated with Adaptive Cards\n9. Bot Service translates response BACK to channel-\nnative format:\n   • Slack: Block Kit JSON (Adaptive Cards → Block Kit\nmapper)\n   • Facebook: Generic/Button templates\n   • IVR: SSML text-to-speech via Azure Speech Service\n10. Channel adapter delivers response to user\n\nCorner case: Card fallback — if channel doesn’t support\nAdaptive Cards,\nrenderer degrades to plain text + button list\nCorner case: IVR timeout — 30s silence → \"Are you still\nthere?\" prompt,\n60s → disconnect + save transcript to Dataverse",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "flow_omni",
      "originalText": "OMNICHANNEL FLOW (Slack / Facebook / IVR)\nStep-by-Step:\n\n1. User sends message on Slack/FB/phone\n2. Channel adapter receives via per-channel webhook\n   • Slack: Events API POST (JSON payload)\n   • Facebook: Messenger webhook (PAGE_TOKEN)\n   • IVR: Azure Communication Services (SIP trunk)\n3. Adapter normalizes to Bot Framework Activity schema\n   • Activity.type = \"message\"\n   • Activity.channelId = \"slack\" | \"facebook\" | \"telephony\"\n   • Attachments mapped to BF Attachment schema\n4. Normalized Activity → Azure Bot Service (HTTPS/443)\n5. Bot Service routes to Bot Runtime Gateway (by bot registration ID)\n6. Gateway loads session from Redis (key: session:{botId}:{convId})\n   • If new conversation: create session, load bot config from Dataverse\n   • If existing: resume dialog state from Redis\n7. Dialog Engine executes (same pipeline as Teams)\n8. Response Activity generated with Adaptive Cards\n9. Bot Service translates response BACK to channel-native format:\n   • Slack: Block Kit JSON (Adaptive Cards → Block Kit mapper)\n   • Facebook: Generic/Button templates\n   • IVR: SSML text-to-speech via Azure Speech Service\n10. Channel adapter delivers response to user\n\nCorner case: Card fallback — if channel doesn’t support Adaptive Cards,\nrenderer degrades to plain text + button list\nCorner case: IVR timeout — 30s silence → \"Are you still there?\" prompt,\n60s → disconnect + save transcript to Dataverse",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "syncedAt": "2026-07-18T12:43:10.902Z",
      "source": "frontend_sync",
      "syncTimestamp": "2026-07-18T12:43:10.887Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "inWBf2ckeogsLLB9GqH_W",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -451.7407903051801,
      "y": 1514.3076249886617,
      "width": 486.71966552734375,
      "height": 1025,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2j",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1106035589,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 907039275,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784374947575,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "WEB CHAT FLOW (Embedded Widget)\nStep-by-Step:\n\n1. Website loads Copilot Studio web chat widget\n   • <iframe> embed or React component\n(botframework-webchat)\n   • JS SDK fetches Direct Line token: POST\n/v3/directline/tokens\n   • Token scoped to specific bot ID, 30 min\nTTL\n2. User types message in widget\n3. SDK sends to Direct Line API (WebSocket or\nREST polling)\n   • WebSocket:\nwss://directline.botframework.com/v3/directline\n   • REST: POST /v3/directline/conversations/\n{id}/activities\n4. Direct Line → Bot Service → Bot Runtime\nGateway\n5. Gateway processes (same pipeline: Redis\nsession → Dialog → AI)\n6. Response streamed back via Direct Line\nWebSocket\n7. Widget renders Adaptive Cards natively (full\nv1.5 support)\n\nAuth options:\n• Anonymous (no sign-in, limited data access)\n• SSO (Entra ID popup/redirect, delegated Graph\naccess)\n• Magic code (6-digit OTP for identity\nverification)\n\nCorner case: Token expiry mid-conversation →\nSDK auto-refreshes\nvia /v3/directline/tokens/refresh (silent, no user\ndisruption)\nCorner case: CSP (Content Security Policy)\nblocking iframe →\ncustomer must whitelist *.botframework.com in\nCSP headers",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "flow_webchat",
      "originalText": "WEB CHAT FLOW (Embedded Widget)\nStep-by-Step:\n\n1. Website loads Copilot Studio web chat widget\n   • <iframe> embed or React component (botframework-webchat)\n   • JS SDK fetches Direct Line token: POST /v3/directline/tokens\n   • Token scoped to specific bot ID, 30 min TTL\n2. User types message in widget\n3. SDK sends to Direct Line API (WebSocket or REST polling)\n   • WebSocket: wss://directline.botframework.com/v3/directline\n   • REST: POST /v3/directline/conversations/{id}/activities\n4. Direct Line → Bot Service → Bot Runtime Gateway\n5. Gateway processes (same pipeline: Redis session → Dialog → AI)\n6. Response streamed back via Direct Line WebSocket\n7. Widget renders Adaptive Cards natively (full v1.5 support)\n\nAuth options:\n• Anonymous (no sign-in, limited data access)\n• SSO (Entra ID popup/redirect, delegated Graph access)\n• Magic code (6-digit OTP for identity verification)\n\nCorner case: Token expiry mid-conversation → SDK auto-refreshes\nvia /v3/directline/tokens/refresh (silent, no user disruption)\nCorner case: CSP (Content Security Policy) blocking iframe →\ncustomer must whitelist *.botframework.com in CSP headers",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "syncedAt": "2026-07-18T12:43:10.902Z",
      "source": "frontend_sync",
      "syncTimestamp": "2026-07-18T12:43:10.887Z"
    },
